{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310624,"nonce":"O8KeDBSka/aoKiesa7YAgxKjfqU=","title":"FIXED 7b496f33: a generic scalar field assigned from an UNTYPED constructor parameter stores the box ADDRESS. `class Node\u003cK,V\u003e { var key:K ...","message":"The emitter was the erased-field store in the lvalue write path: when the field\nslot is `I64` (an erased type parameter) and the value register is anything\nelse, it emitted `build_cast`. A `*void` source is a BOXED value, so the cast\nstored the box address.\n\n**Why the obvious fix is wrong, and this is the real lesson.** Coercing every\n`*void` unconditionally fixes `\u003cInt,Int\u003e` and BREAKS `\u003cString,Int\u003e`: the same\nlowered body serves both. Monomorphization runs AFTER lowering, and the template\nand its specialisation have BYTE-IDENTICAL bodies — verified by dumping both.\nSo lowering cannot statically tell a boxed number from a reference here. Any\nfuture fix at that site faces the same wall.\n\nThe discrimination is therefore at runtime, on the tag:\n`haxe_unbox_scalar_or_addr` (runtime type_system) unwraps only a DynamicValue\ntagged `TYPE_INT`/`TYPE_BOOL` and returns the address untouched otherwise.\n\n**Do NOT reuse `haxe_coerce_dynamic_to_int` for this.** Its heuristic accepts\n`tid \u003e 100 \u0026\u0026 tid \u003c u32::MAX - 10` as a box, which matches CLASS ids — it\nunboxed a String as a number and produced `ssum=0` in\n`test_balancedtree_crossmodule_mono`. That regression is the reason the strict\nvariant exists.\n\nRuled out earlier and still not the site: `coerce_to_i64`, `IrBuilder::build_store`,\nthe int↔float `needs_coerce` cast.\n\n---\n\n`compiler/tests/haxe/test_generic_ctor_untyped_selfref.hx` prints\n`FAIL h_leaf=1 h_parent=2`. The heights are RIGHT, so the SIGILL/monomorphization\nregression that test was written for is still fixed. What fails is the rest of\nthe assertion — `leaf.key == 1 \u0026\u0026 parent.value == 20`:\n\n    h_leaf=1 h_parent=2 leaf.key=1338369136 leaf.value=1338369120\n                        parent.key=1338369088 parent.value=1338369072\n\nThose are addresses. Shape (mirrors `haxe.ds.TreeNode`):\n\n```haxe\nclass TreeNode\u003cK, V\u003e {\n    public var key:K;\n    public var value:V;\n    public function new(l, k, v, r, h = -1) { left = l; key = k; value = v; ... }\n}\nnew TreeNode\u003cInt, Int\u003e(null, 1, 10, null)\n```\n\nMonomorphised ctor `new__i64_i64`, all params `*void` (untyped params erase):\n\n    $6  = call fn280019($1)          ; haxe_unbox_reference_ptr  -\u003e left  CORRECT\n    $13 = gep i64 $0, [$12]          ; key slot, correctly typed i64\n    $14 = cast *void $2 to i64       ; BITCAST of the box pointer  \u003c-- BUG\n    store $13, $14\n\nReference fields get `haxe_unbox_reference_ptr`; scalar fields get a raw\npointer→int cast. The right call exists and is used elsewhere in the same\nfunction: `haxe_coerce_dynamic_to_int` (fn280018) is applied to the `h`\nparameter, and its comment says it handles a boxed DynamicValue AND a\ntype-erased raw integer, so it is safe on either.\n\n- `coerce_to_i64` (hir_to_mir ~38949). Patched it to unbox an erased source,\n  both with a strict `Some(Ptr|Any)` guard and with a widened \"not known-scalar\"\n  guard. **MIR unchanged in both cases** (`cast *void $2 to i64` still emitted),\n  output still garbage. Not on this path. Change reverted.\n- `IrBuilder::build_store` (builder.rs:219) — records `store_ty` from the value\n  register and emits no cast.\n- hir_to_mir:5679 — that cast is gated on `needs_coerce`, which only matches\n  int↔float pairs, so it cannot produce Ptr→i64.\n\nThe emitter computes the field GEP with the field's IR type and then casts the\nvalue to it. Find the constructor/field-assignment lowering that pairs\n`build_gep` + `build_cast(value, .., field_ir_ty)` + `build_store`. Note the\nstore is immediately followed by a read-back (`$17 = load i64 $16`), which\nresembles the anonymous-object storage pattern, so the anon/dynamic field path\nis worth checking even though the field here is a real class field.\n\nFix shape once found: when the source register is not known-scalar and the\ntarget slot is scalar, call `haxe_coerce_dynamic_to_int` /\n`haxe_coerce_dynamic_to_float` instead of casting — the same treatment\nreference fields already get.\n\n`run_haxe_tests.sh` decided PASS from the exit code alone, so this\nself-checking test printed FAIL and was counted green. Fixed in 63463e7c: a\nmarker at column 0 now fails the run (test_rayzor_spec's intentional indented\n\"FAIL\" line still passes). Same family as\n[[bugs_std_string_dynamic_unbox_and_erased_generics]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_generic_scalar_field_stores_box_pointer` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}